<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49072" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trĭfārĭam</span></b>  (collat.
		form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trĭfārĭē</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Diom. p. 279</span></i> P.), adv.
		trifarius, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>triply</i>, <i>in three places</i>
			(not ante-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trifariam adortus castra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					3, 22, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">muniebant Romani,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					5, 26, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">distraxere exercitum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					26, 41, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">epulas dispertire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Vit. 13</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Triply</i>, <i>in a threefold
			manner</i>, <i>in three ways</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">destruitur propositio trifariam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Dogm. Plat. 3, p. 32, 24</span></i>
			.</div>
